Title:
Pass-the-Passkey Family of Attacks

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
- A SpecterOps repository containing tools and documentation for assessing “Pass-the-Passkey” attacks targeting WebAuthn/FIDO2 passkey authentication on Windows.  
- It focuses on capturing, replaying, and tampering with WebAuthn assertion flows to evaluate real-world weaknesses in passkey-based logins (including synced passkeys from password managers).  
- Key components include a WebView2-based “Passkey Injector” for intercepting and injecting WebAuthn assertion JSON, and “SharpPasskeys” (a .NET Framework payload) intended for execution via C2 to prompt users for passkey auth and collect resulting assertions.  
- A native “WebAuthn Hook” DLL uses Microsoft Detours to intercept the Win32 WebAuthn API (`WebAuthNAuthenticatorGetAssertion`) and communicates via a named pipe for monitoring/modifying challenges and assertions.  
- The repo also references DSInternals tooling for WebAuthn API interaction and passkey registration workflows (Entra ID/Okta), plus scripts to chain captured assertions into Entra ID token acquisition.  
- Useful primarily for red teams, pentesters, and security researchers validating passkey deployments; also relevant to defenders for understanding interception points and telemetry opportunities.

Technical Focus:
- WebAuthn/FIDO2 assertion interception and injection
- Win32 WebAuthn API hooking (`WebAuthNAuthenticatorGetAssertion`) with Microsoft Detours
- Browser process injection + IPC via named pipes (`\\.\pipe\WebAuthnHook`)
- Replay/phishing-style forwarding of assertions and challenge manipulation
- Entra ID passkey-based sign-in and OAuth token retrieval (Microsoft Graph)
- Windows Hello credential enumeration and Event Log monitoring

Use Cases:
- Test server-side WebAuthn validation by injecting modified assertions/challenges
- Replay captured WebAuthn assertions from logs/hooks/traffic to assess anti-replay controls
- Simulate passkey phishing/relay scenarios by forwarding attacker-controlled assertions
- Validate risk of stolen synced passkeys (Bitwarden/KeePassXC/1Password) in enterprise SSO
- Collect WebAuthn assertions via C2 payload execution for controlled assessments
- Analyze WebAuthn extensions/features used by specific cloud identity providers

Keywords:
WebAuthn, FIDO2, passkeys, Windows Hello, assertion, PublicKeyCredential, challenge, Edge WebView2, WebView2, Microsoft Detours, API hooking, WebAuthNAuthenticatorGetAssertion, DLL injection, named pipe, Entra ID, Okta, OAuth tokens, Microsoft Graph, Mythic C2, Apollo agent